// Disk Format

Sector 0: Filesystem Information
    [Offset, Length] Field

    [0, 4] Sectors in Volume - 1 (Max LBA in Volume) (Max 2^32 or 2TB of data) = a
    [4, 4] Sectors per Bitmap (Should be the Sectors in Volume divided by 4096 ((a+1)/4096)) = b
    [8, 4] Sectors per Root Directory

Sectors 1 to b: Bitmap

Sectors b+1 to a: Data (Start with Root Directory)

// Directory Entry
[Offset, Length] Field

[0, 1] Flags: 0x1 = Directory, 0x02 = Executable, 0x04 = Read Only, 0x08 = User Readable, 0x10 = User Writable (Overrided by Read Only)
[1, 29] Name
[30, 2] Last Sector Bytes Used 
[32, 4] Start LBA
[36, 4] Length in Sectors
[40, 8] Created Date Unix Time Extented
[48, 8] Modified Date
[56, 8] Accessed Date